    "result_text": "Full suite green: **46 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the \"reject future registration date\" rule for `POST /api/owners`, following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions.\n\n**What I added:**\n\n1. **`RequireRegistrationDateNotFuture`** (function) \u2014 reads the validated body via `@Val OwnerFieldsDto` and throws when a *supplied* `registrationDate` is later than `LocalDate.now()`. An absent date is left untouched (it still defaults to the server date in `BuildOwner`).\n\n2. **`OwnerRegistrationDateInvalidException`** (checked exception) \u2014 carries the offending date so it appears in a `throws` clause and routes to an escalation handler.\n\n3. **`OwnerRegistrationDateInvalidExceptionHandler`** \u2014 responds `400` with `{\"errors\":[\"registrationDate\"]}`, mirroring the existing `OwnerPostcodeInvalidExceptionHandler`.\n\n4. **Escalation YAML** mapping the exception to the handler.\n\n5. **Wired the step** into `owners.POST.yml` between `require` (which publishes the body) and `postcode`, under the same `transaction` governance \u2014 so a future date is rejected before anything is built or stored.\n\n**Why this placement:** the check must run after `RequireOwnerFields` publishes the body as a variable (it reads `@Val`), and before `BuildOwner`, so an invalid date is a clean 400 and never persisted.\n\nThe new `Cp33Tests.errorRejectsFutureDate` (posting `registrationDate: \"2999-01-01\"`) now returns 400, while past/today dates (e.g. `Cp07Tests`' `2026-01-03` and the business-day cases) still create successfully.",
